can all demons together defeat muzon  which ones would pose the most threat to  him and which ones would be defeated in  a matter of seconds well firstly i think  we can all agree that normal demons  would pose no threat to muzon as they  can be easily eliminated even by amateur  demon slayers because of this let's  primarily focus on demon moons despite  being insanely powerful the 12 kizuki  would face a great deal of trouble while  battling muzon during the sunrise  countdown arc all heshira's and tonjro  combined barely succeeded in defeating  him the biggest reason they managed to  pull off such a colossal feat was due to  tamayo's help tomeo was well aware of  muzon's strength as she had spent a good  amount of time with him therefore she  came prepared with a poison strong  enough to weaken muzon significantly  allowing the hashiris to fight him in  somewhat fair conditions muzon is quite  literally invincible and if he fought  the demon slayers in his full power he  would easily obliterate them keeping  this in mind there is absolutely no way  that the demon moons could defeat him he  would probably crush them all in a  matter of minutes alright the answer to  that question was pretty obvious but  what would happen if demon moons fought  muzon in his poisoned state would it be  any different muzon isn't just powerful  in terms of physical strength he's the  king for a reason as he is the one who  created the army of demons additionally  all demons are made from muzon cells  which means that he has complete control  over them the cells act as a  double-edged sword offering great  strength to the demons but at the same  time making them vulnerable to muzon in  season two of the anime when akaza  visits muzon to inform him about the  mujin train incident the demon king is  pretty furious at him in his fury with  just one look muzon inflicted immense  damage to the poor demon for a demon as  strong as a kaza to take so much damage  with just one look speaks volumes from  muson's capabilities this basically  implies that the demon king no matter  how weakened he is by injuries or even  poison can defeat any demon in a matter  of seconds so if we wanted to make this  comparison realistic and fair we would  have to strip muzon of his ability to  control other demons only then can the  demon moons have a fair fight with the  demon king therefore let's take away the  specific ability of muzon for a second  and compare how each demon would fare  against him in a fight which ones would  be able to hold their ground and fight  for a long time and which ones would die  quickly would any of them be able to  inflict any damage on muzon at all first  of all we'll not include average demons  and lower moons in this comparison since  as we already stated they're just too  weak and wouldn't make any significant  difference in the fight the first upper  moons would be gyotora and daki the two  siblings have two advantages one is  gyotoro's blades giving him significant  crowd control over muzon's tentacles and  the other one is the fact that they need  to be decapitated at the same time in  order to kill them muzon's tentacles are  pretty strong and having the ability to  take care of them is a considerable  advantage unfortunately gyotoro lacks  speed and strength required to battle a  powerful adversary like muzon what's  more daki is his weakness and even muzon  believes that gyotaro can do much better  without her all in all both of the  siblings will be killed fairly quickly  next is upper moon 5 gyoko yoko has some  really strong abilities such as  teleportation and spawning large fish  monsters from his pots considering the  fact that gyoko has been on muzon's side  for a long time the demon king is well  aware of his tricks and techniques  joko's abilities may work on someone who  has no information about him but for the  demon king he's a piece of cake muzon  would easily destroy his pots quickly  defeating the upper moon 5 demon moving  forward the upper rank 4 also has a very  impressive skill set which might just  help him last a bit longer in a fight  against muzon than the previously  mentioned demons hontangu can manipulate  his flesh at will allowing him to  increase or decrease his size and make  clones of himself each time he is  decapitated this is a very useful skill  to possess and considering the fact that  ontango is one of the stealthiest and  fastest demons in the upper moons he  might just be able to prolong his life  against muzon and even dodge some of his  attacks as well however at the end of  the day muzon can still easily beat him  his flesh manipulation may be bothersome  but it would only mean that muzon would  have to spend a little more time  battling him what's more he doesn't  possess enough strength to actually deal  any significant damage to the demon king  alright here's where things begin to get  serious with the next challenger being  the one and only akaza the upper rank 3  would definitely pose some problems for  the demon king and let me explain why  akasa was insanely strong even as a  human and now as a demon he is on a  completely different level his sole  weakness is the selfless state ability  possessed only by a few demon slayers  this power when awakened can prevent  akaza from sensing his opponent's  fighting spirit making him useless in a  fight however this ability is unique to  the demon slayers only meaning that  muzon would not be able to hide his  presence from a kaza what's more he also  possesses the ability which allows him  to pinpoint his foes weaknesses all of  that coupled with his exceptional  martial art skills and speed would  definitely allow him to land a few blows  on muzon due to his experience and  overall much greater strength in akaza  muzon would obviously win the fight  eventually but not without a few  scratches so if akaza managed to land  some hits on muzon how would doma fare  against him it's pretty unfortunate that  we weren't shown the full extent of  doma's powers and capabilities in the  manga however based on what we have seen  doma is not to be underestimated as he  is a staggeringly powerful foe an  essential point to note is that he  doesn't really have any known weakness  this would make it much harder for muzon  to deal with him the only reason doma  lost in the manga was because of his  careless attitude and the poison he  consumed shinobu had been consuming the  wisteria flower in minor amounts for  over a year and even then doma didn't  die from absorbing her in any case he  would not have to worry about the poison  in a battle against muzon and he would  definitely not underestimate the demon  king one bit the upper rank 2 possesses  perception mobility and strength that  far surpasses those of the demons  mentioned before even his blood demon  art is quite impressive and allows him  to manipulate his flesh and blood to  create ice and frost using these  techniques doma can deal significant  damage and possibly freeze muzon  therefore he would definitely put up a  good fight and would stand his ground  the longest but would eventually lose  finally let's talk about the one who  would really give moves on a tough time  the upper moon one kokushibo now the  fight between the two would be very  interesting indeed considering how  unbelievably strong they are but that's  not the main point here the reason why  it would be pretty different from other  fights so far is kokoshibo's ability to  regenerate his head while decapitated  this power was witnessed in his fight  against the hashiris during the infinity  castle arc akasa could also regenerate  his head but i'm only mentioning  kokoshibo because akaza's regeneration  was much slower and he gave up midway on  the other hand kokoshibo managed to  fully regenerate his head in a matter of  seconds this would play a massive role  in his fight against demon king and  would mean that even when muzon  decapitates him kokoshibo will survive  and continue to fight additionally  kokoshibo is the only demon capable of  using breathing techniques which makes  him all the more dangerous his moon  breathing combined with impeccable  swordsmanship would give muzon a pretty  tough time a point to note about his  regenerative abilities is that he only  managed to regenerate his head once  during the fight with the shiras he may  be able to do it multiple times but we  can't be sure of that therefore if  muslin slashes his head multiple times  he would probably not be able to recover  in time and ultimately the fight would  end in the demon king's favor but it  would definitely take some time and now  the final question what if all upper  moons fought him together in general  each upper moon is usually as strong as  a hashira some of them are even more  powerful comparable to the strength of  two or more pillars even shinobu agreed  with this statement therefore we can say  that this would be similar to muzon  fighting a dozen hashiras at the same  time which is more than he fought during  the sunrise countdown arc this would be  the greatest battle of all demon slayer  history and muzon will not be able to  get out of this one easily the fight  would be much longer with all seven of  the upper moon demons working together  gradually weakening the demon lord and  tiring him out the upper moons would be  at a significant advantage due to their  strength and unique abilities which they  can combine to inflict massive damage on  muzon at the very beginning of the fight  the demon king would act quickly to take  care of the weaker upper moons like yoko  daki and yuutaro before they are killed  gyoko and kyotaro would use their  special poisoning techniques on muzon it  wouldn't do much at the time but in the  long run it may weaken him a bit  furthermore as time goes on akaza and  kokoshiba would deal a lot of physical  damage to muzon at the same time domo  would use his powerful blood demon art  and the powdered ice to poison muzon  even more the fight would begin to wear  the demon king down weakening him to the  point that the upper moons now have a  slight advantage over him eventually  near the end of the night the upper  moons would have wounded him enough to  decapitate him and the one to do it  would be none other than the strongest  of them all kogoshibo however let's not  forget that muzon is capable of  regenerating his head making him immune  to death by decapitation although he  wouldn't die regenerating his head would  wear down muzon considerably making it  extremely hard for him to kill the  remaining demons the battle would  eventually come to an end with the sun  rising and burning all the demons  including muzon to ashes therefore the  end of this incredibly long and  impressive fight would be a tie and none  of them would be standing victorious at  the end click on this video where we  explained what would happen if yurishi  became a demon don't be shy click it
 

